Lab 13: Configure Load Balancing for VM Services
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Create Kubernetes Services for Virtual Machines running in OpenShift Virtualization
Configure different types of load balancing services (ClusterIP, NodePort, and LoadBalancer)
Test load balancing functionality with multiple VM instances
Understand how OpenShift networking integrates with virtualized workloads
Implement service discovery and traffic distribution for VM-based applications
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Kubernetes concepts (Pods, Services, Deployments)
Familiarity with OpenShift CLI (oc command)
Knowledge of YAML configuration files
Understanding of networking concepts (IP addresses, ports, load balancing)
Experience with Linux command line operations
Completion of previous OpenShift Virtualization labs or equivalent knowledge
