Task 2: Configure Load Balancing Services
Subtask 2.1: Create a ClusterIP Service
ClusterIP services provide internal load balancing within the cluster.

Create a ClusterIP service configuration:
cat > clusterip-service.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: webserver-clusterip
  namespace: default
  labels:
    app: webserver
spec:
  type: ClusterIP
  selector:
    app: webserver
  ports:
  - name: http
    port: 80
    targetPort: 80
    protocol: TCP
  sessionAffinity: None
EOF
Apply the ClusterIP service:
oc apply -f clusterip-service.yaml
Verify the service creation:
oc get svc webserver-clusterip
Get detailed service information:
oc describe svc webserver-clusterip
Subtask 2.2: Create a NodePort Service
NodePort services expose the application on each node's IP at a static port.

Create a NodePort service configuration:
cat > nodeport-service.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: webserver-nodeport
  namespace: default
  labels:
    app: webserver
spec:
  type: NodePort
  selector:
    app: webserver
  ports:
  - name: http
    port: 80
    targetPort: 80
    nodePort: 30080
    protocol: TCP
  sessionAffinity: None
EOF
Apply the NodePort service:
oc apply -f nodeport-service.yaml
Verify the NodePort service:
oc get svc webserver-nodeport
Subtask 2.3: Create a LoadBalancer Service
LoadBalancer services provide external load balancing (when supported by the cloud provider).

Create a LoadBalancer service configuration:
cat > loadbalancer-service.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: webserver-loadbalancer
  namespace: default
  labels:
    app: webserver
spec:
  type: LoadBalancer
  selector:
    app: webserver
  ports:
  - name: http
    port: 80
    targetPort: 80
    protocol: TCP
  sessionAffinity: None
EOF
Apply the LoadBalancer service:
oc apply -f loadbalancer-service.yaml
Check all services:
oc get svc -l app=webserver
Task 3: Test Load Balancing Functionality
Subtask 3.1: Test ClusterIP Service
Create a test pod to access the ClusterIP service:
cat > test-pod.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: test-client
  namespace: default
spec:
  containers:
  - name: client
    image: registry.access.redhat.com/ubi8/ubi:latest
    command: ["/bin/bash"]
    args: ["-c", "sleep 3600"]
  restartPolicy: Never
EOF
Apply the test pod:
oc apply -f test-pod.yaml
Wait for the test pod to be ready:
oc wait --for=condition=Ready pod/test-client --timeout=60s
Test the ClusterIP service from within the cluster:
oc exec test-client -- curl -s http://webserver-clusterip
Test multiple requests to see load balancing in action:
for i in {1..10}; do
  echo "Request $i:"
  oc exec test-client -- curl -s http://webserver-clusterip | grep -E "(VM1|VM2)"
  sleep 1
done
Subtask 3.2: Test NodePort Service
Get the node IP addresses:
oc get nodes -o wide
Test the NodePort service (replace NODE_IP with actual node IP):
NODE_IP=$(oc get nodes -o jsonpath='{.items[0].status.addresses[?(@.type=="InternalIP")].address}')
echo "Testing NodePort service at $NODE_IP:30080"
Test from the test pod:
oc exec test-client -- curl -s http://$NODE_IP:30080
Test multiple requests:
for i in {1..5}; do
  echo "NodePort Request $i:"
  oc exec test-client -- curl -s http://$NODE_IP:30080 | grep -E "(VM1|VM2)"
  sleep 1
done
Subtask 3.3: Verify Load Distribution
Check service endpoints:
oc get endpoints webserver-clusterip
oc get endpoints webserver-nodeport
oc get endpoints webserver-loadbalancer
Get detailed endpoint information:
oc describe endpoints webserver-clusterip
Monitor VM network traffic (optional):
oc get vmis -o wide
Subtask 3.4: Test Service Discovery
Test DNS resolution for services:
oc exec test-client -- nslookup webserver-clusterip
oc exec test-client -- nslookup webserver-nodeport
Test service environment variables:
oc exec test-client -- env | grep WEBSERVER
Task 4: Advanced Load Balancing Configuration
Subtask 4.1: Configure Session Affinity
Create a service with session affinity:
cat > session-affinity-service.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: webserver-sticky
  namespace: default
  labels:
    app: webserver
spec:
  type: ClusterIP
  selector:
    app: webserver
  ports:
  - name: http
    port: 80
    targetPort: 80
    protocol: TCP
  sessionAffinity: ClientIP
  sessionAffinityConfig:
    clientIP:
      timeoutSeconds: 300
EOF
Apply the session affinity service:
oc apply -f session-affinity-service.yaml
Test session affinity:
for i in {1..5}; do
  echo "Sticky Session Request $i:"
  oc exec test-client -- curl -s http://webserver-sticky | grep -E "(VM1|VM2)"
  sleep 1
done
Subtask 4.2: Configure Health Checks
Create a service with health check annotations:
cat > health-check-service.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: webserver-health
  namespace: default
  labels:
    app: webserver
  annotations:
    service.alpha.kubernetes.io/tolerate-unready-endpoints: "true"
spec:
  type: ClusterIP
  selector:
    app: webserver
  ports:
  - name: http
    port: 80
    targetPort: 80
    protocol: TCP
  publishNotReadyAddresses: false
EOF
Apply the health check service:
oc apply -f health-check-service.yaml
